\begin{aligned}
\sin \theta &=\frac{\lambda}{d}=\frac{589 \times 10^{-9}}{0.589 \times 10^{-3}}=10^{-3} \\
\Rightarrow \quad \theta &=\sin ^{-1}(0.001)
